so like I said in terms of mental health  I suppose is one of those things that  all of our health fluctuates you know at  different points in our lives and I  suppose exam time is a stressful time  for everyone in matter what I think for  anybody that you know does kind of  suffer with anxiety exams are likely to  be a kind of a really big trigger for  that and revision can be a very  difficult time sometimes as well because  sometimes you have to be sat at your  desk for long periods you might not be  interacting so much with friends or  doing all the kind of things that make  us feel well like you know hobbies or  sports or being outside and getting  fresh air all the things that do kind of  keep our well-being in a good place  are harder to keep up during the  revision period so it is a sort of time  when I think you know people can feel  like they're struggling a lot more and  obviously the pressure of the exams come  closer and closer as well as it's quite  scary do it so if people feel that they  are struggling with with anxiety or if  they feel like they are just being  cooped up and they're not working at  their best and they're not feeling at  their best what's the best thing that  they can do so I think it's very  difficult to tear yourself away from  revision when there's so much to do but  a good advice really is to try and if  you have a schedule and you have you  know timeframes mapped out when you want  to be studying try and include in that  schedule things like you know just  getting out and doing something that you  enjoy also include things like 10-minute  break every hour or so you're studying  because actually we only have so much  concentration anyway and past that point  you can't really memorize what you're  learn learning you're not really  focusing properly and actually that can  become really stressful in itself so  it's much better to have a 10-minute  break where you just completely take  yourself away from that situation so get  away from the computer away from your  desk try and maybe go for a brisk walk  will do something like active or meet a  friend so you can kind of take your mind  away as well  as your body from that stressful kind of  experience and then I suppose the next  level of severity if people feel like  that they are really struggling and you  know maybe it might be getting a bit too  much hell they might need to delay an  exam or you know that level of severity  what then should they do  they get in contact with work being it  might be getting good I did to get in  contact with well-being at that time  because we can think about whether  there's any support that that student  you know might be able to access that  might be helpful if a student wanted to  defer an exam what departments normally  ask for is a letter from the GP as  medical evidence whether typically would  say that they they feel that students  not in the best place to take the exam  currently and then I think each  department might have different  processes for how they go through that  and then I think the exams are normally  in August that have been deferred if a  student kind of thinks that they want to  want to do the exams and then it gets  really close to the time and they change  their mind I think they have to the best  thing to do is to get a GPS note on the  day of the exam that they need to go in  and file with the department and say  that they'd like to try and mitigate for  those exams which means they'll be able  to extend have an extension unto them  and it is possible to do that so it's  not a completely other question if the  problem is severe enough it's not  something to be taken lightly but if  people really feel like they're  struggling it's an option it's an option  yeah and I always encourage students to  talk to their department office or their  tutors about these things because like I  say there are different processes with  different departments so really good  just to get that information and just  get all the options and the kind of  processes involved so they know they  know what's work you know there's a lot  of different kind of emotional  difficulties that we would work with or  just if people are feeling a bit  stressed and feel like things are  difficult and then they're kind of  struggling to cope with the workload we  can work with all sorts of different  difficulties which is why we're with the  well-being center
 

